WEBVTT

00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:12.275
Confundus.

00:00:24.766 --> 00:00:26.768
[CHEERING]

00:00:28.247 --> 00:00:30.554
Isn't he brilliant?

00:00:33.339 --> 00:00:37.169
I have to admit, I thought
I was gonna miss that last one.

00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:40.346
I hope Cormac's
not taking it too hard.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.525
He's got a bit of a thing
for you, Hermione. Cormac.

00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:46.527
He's vile.

00:00:51.357 --> 00:00:53.795
HARRY:
Have you ever heard
of this spell? Sectumsempra?

00:00:53.838 --> 00:00:56.101
No, I haven't.

00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:57.842
And if you had a shred
of self-respect,

00:00:57.886 --> 00:00:59.409
you'd hand that book in.

00:00:59.452 --> 00:01:02.020
Not bloody likely.
He's top of the class.

00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:03.848
He's even better than you,
Hermione.

00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:06.155
Slughorn thinks he's a genius.

00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:09.462
What?

00:01:09.506 --> 00:01:12.378
I'd like to know whose that
book was. Let's have a look.

00:01:12.422 --> 00:01:13.858
No.

00:01:15.425 --> 00:01:17.166
Why not?

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:18.950
The binding is fragile.

00:01:18.994 --> 00:01:21.866
The binding is fragile?Yeah.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.912
[♪♪♪]

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.568
Who's the Half-Blood Prince?Who?

00:01:27.611 --> 00:01:29.134
That's what
it says right here:

00:01:29.178 --> 00:01:31.528
"This book is property
of the Half-Blood Prince."

00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:50.852
HERMIONE:
For weeks you carry around
this book,

00:01:50.895 --> 00:01:52.549
practically sleep with it

00:01:52.593 --> 00:01:54.638
and yet you have no desire
to find out who he is?

00:01:54.682 --> 00:01:58.250
HARRY:
I didn't say I wasn't curious,
and I don't sleep with it.

00:01:58.294 --> 00:01:59.643
RON:
Well, it's true.

00:01:59.687 --> 00:02:01.253
I like a nice chat
before I go to bed.

00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:03.386
Now all you do is read
that bloody book.

00:02:03.429 --> 00:02:05.475
It's just like being
with Hermione.

00:02:06.781 --> 00:02:09.348
HERMIONE:
Well, I was curious,
so I went to--

00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:12.787
The library.The library. And?

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.615
And nothing.

00:02:14.658 --> 00:02:17.618
I couldn't find a reference
anywhere to a Half-Blood Prince.

00:02:17.661 --> 00:02:19.402
There we go.
That settles it, then.

00:02:19.445 --> 00:02:22.100
Filius! I was hoping to find
you in the Three Broomsticks.

00:02:22.144 --> 00:02:26.496
Uh, no, emergency choir
practice, I'm afraid, Horace.

00:02:30.761 --> 00:02:33.329
Does anyone fancy
a Butterbeer?

00:02:33.372 --> 00:02:35.940
A chum of mine
was sledging down Claxby Hill.

00:02:35.984 --> 00:02:39.683
We had a very long, homemade,
Norwegian-style sledge.

00:02:39.727 --> 00:02:42.338
HARRY:
No, not there. Over here.

00:02:42.381 --> 00:02:44.514
No, sit beside me.

00:02:46.168 --> 00:02:47.778
Okay.

00:02:48.953 --> 00:02:50.389
MAN:
Something to drink?

00:02:50.433 --> 00:02:51.913
HERMIONE:
Um, three Butterbeers,

00:02:51.956 --> 00:02:53.654
and some ginger in mine, please.

00:02:58.528 --> 00:03:00.530
[SLUGHORN SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY]

00:03:04.752 --> 00:03:06.797
Oh, bloody hell.

00:03:09.713 --> 00:03:11.759
Slick git.

00:03:11.802 --> 00:03:14.675
Honestly, Ronald,
they're only holding hands.

00:03:17.025 --> 00:03:18.722
And snogging.

00:03:18.766 --> 00:03:22.378
I'd like to leave.What?

00:03:22.421 --> 00:03:24.119
You can't be serious.

00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:26.687
That happens to be my sister.So?

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.863
What if she looked over here
and saw you snogging me?

00:03:28.906 --> 00:03:30.734
Would you expect her to leave?

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:33.128
SLUGHORN:
Hey, my boy.

00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:34.695
Hello, sir.
Wonderful to see you.

00:03:34.738 --> 00:03:36.697
And you, and you.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.611
So, what brings you here?

00:03:38.655 --> 00:03:40.309
The Three Broomsticks
and I go way back,

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:43.529
further than I care to admit.

00:03:43.573 --> 00:03:45.618
I can remember when
it was One Broomstick.

00:03:45.662 --> 00:03:47.142
[LAUGHING]

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:48.404
All hands on deck, Granger.

00:03:48.447 --> 00:03:50.623
Listen, my boy,
in the old days

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:54.236
I used to throw together
the occasional supper party

00:03:54.279 --> 00:03:56.542
for the select student or two.

00:03:56.586 --> 00:03:57.543
Would you be game?

00:03:57.587 --> 00:04:00.677
I'd consider it an honor, sir.

00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:03.549
You would be welcome too,
Granger.

00:04:03.593 --> 00:04:06.378
I'd be delighted, sir.

00:04:06.422 --> 00:04:08.729
Splendid. Look for my owl.

00:04:10.774 --> 00:04:12.689
Good to see you, Wallenby.

00:04:17.476 --> 00:04:19.304
What are you playing at?

00:04:20.958 --> 00:04:23.439
Dumbledore's asked me
to get to know him.

00:04:23.482 --> 00:04:25.571
Get to know him?
I don't know.

00:04:25.615 --> 00:04:27.051
It must be important.

00:04:27.095 --> 00:04:29.488
If it wasn't,
Dumbledore wouldn't ask.

00:04:34.929 --> 00:04:37.192
Got a little bit...

00:04:47.811 --> 00:04:49.813
LEANNE:
Katie, you don't know
what it could be.

00:04:49.857 --> 00:04:51.597
RON [WHISPERING]: Harry.HARRY: What?

00:04:51.641 --> 00:04:53.774
RON:
Did you hear what she
was saying back at the pub

00:04:53.817 --> 00:04:55.863
about me and her snogging?

00:04:55.906 --> 00:04:57.778
As if.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.913
[LEANNE SCREAMS]

00:05:04.132 --> 00:05:07.570
I warned her.
I warned her not to touch it.

00:05:12.836 --> 00:05:13.968
[ROARING]

00:05:28.896 --> 00:05:31.812
Don't get any closer.
Get back, all of you.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.861
Now, now, now, now.

00:05:44.128 --> 00:05:47.001
Do not touch that,
except by the wrappings.

00:05:47.044 --> 00:05:49.177
Do you understand?

